<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nigeria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nigeria is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, created as a British colony in the early twentieth century and independent since 1960. Its territory includes the heartlands of several empires covered on the site, among them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. Nigeria has been central to the debate over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">repatriation</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a> looted by British forces in 1897.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nigeria.jpg" alt="Nigeria" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jon Harald Søby. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Nigeria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
